{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01OU", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-locally-closed-in-Noetherian}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e3601ee5dc26bb909aec58fa06e9818fbaa6d77b912cc39223c0dc65163782bd", "source_text": "Any locally closed subscheme of a (locally) Noetherian\nscheme is (locally) Noetherian.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:82a3d62cdfb37dac37b288593f7b521fcde67f0284f9494c433ecae2b01264ed", "unit_id": "tag:02IK:statement"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01OU", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:9546a5d15171c2a5c0e5b99b7097001615e335897d86534338121c2d599af09d", "source_text": "Omitted. Hint: Any quotient, and any localization of a Noetherian\nring is Noetherian. For the Noetherian case use again\nthat any subset of a Noetherian space is a Noetherian space\n(with induced topology).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:05e374f72e5e9e3c9af11bb48d01ed341ad61f74563b9349446920981d9c47ad", "unit_id": "tag:02IK:proof"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01OU", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-Noetherian-irreducible-components}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:3c08c03ac7bc4d557902f8d3d8dca8dd83d103ce1836e96a147ee3a7a1e04ba2", "source_text": "A Noetherian scheme has a finite number of irreducible components.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d23879f43f1df329660c357ce1abba4a1e20196658c48e4fb0e785925237f22f", "unit_id": "tag:0BA8:statement"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01OU", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-Noetherian-topology}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{topology-lemma-Noetherian}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c98d8eb4a1e0b41d41f81d83a1529844970b7f290232ae035847b30a1c11852b", "source_text": "The underlying topological space of a Noetherian scheme is Noetherian\n(Lemma <REF_0001>)\nand we conclude because a Noetherian topological space\nhas only finitely many irreducible components\n(Topology, Lemma <REF_0002>).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d8598502a7df3bf7debd18d19cc0e26616254f3e3f2b295147df9a8cc1df6054", "unit_id": "tag:0BA8:proof"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01OU", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0002": "$X$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-morphism-Noetherian-schemes-quasi-compact}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:41b44b2b7a26b7671956479184f834369a23fb9f8f49b38fe32949e38ed58c22", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:4613134d180c39ffa6717562c3e5ef430aafc48fe51b0fd762e30bc96bcde4d9", "source_text": "Any morphism of schemes <MATH_0001> with <MATH_0002> Noetherian\nis quasi-compact.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c33d0ad03d1fb15f7a9dba35f73931af46dd1567a209c11fc4874d59a3ffc517", "unit_id": "tag:01P0:statement"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01OU", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-Noetherian-topology}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{topology-lemma-Noetherian}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{topology-lemma-Noetherian-quasi-compact}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:59415f87ec124cba5d64e6f035d00bcacff44a3244fa78067e4ba5e6127145eb", "source_text": "Use Lemma <REF_0001>\nand use that any subset of a Noetherian topological\nspace is quasi-compact (see Topology,\nLemmas <REF_0002> and\n<REF_0003>).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:990355f0ea753985ce069195cb9719a855656955a585fe3191e2010a48b939a9", "unit_id": "tag:01P0:proof"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "01OU", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:1f8ea1b0f6d8f452ba6e1958fbb96f06c1a3b4a44802a50db446d950505d1e7a", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nHere is a fun lemma.\nIt says that every locally Noetherian scheme has plenty of\nclosed points (at least one in every closed subset).\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b99a4463762d8fe62cc5d45ad0b0212b5cf0e86de738fd6650f7390e3c41f74c", "unit_id": "tag:01OU:prose-0003"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01OU", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-locally-Noetherian-closed-point}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c412b91edee14cc4fc1a3c3b070be1b2d3e2e024fe92c7b3fe1443cf347a6452", "source_text": "Any nonempty locally Noetherian scheme has a closed point.\nAny nonempty closed subset of a locally Noetherian scheme has a closed point.\nEquivalently, any point of a locally Noetherian scheme specializes\nto a closed point.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:75770e5d32e4c8ed579be096101050bfc696663e8c7d86e6bdc3aa4d162028c7", "unit_id": "tag:02IL:statement"}
